# Split first, then fix

We spent many hours rebreaking bots by editing the same files for unrelated tickets. Extra files are preferred.

## Before touching a new hack/bot bug

1. Name the **last known-good slice** (spend, caps, Orders open, hijack HP, SHOW RANGE host, …).
2. If it still lives in a mixed file (`RfsHackBeacon.lua`, hijack, `Game.lua`, `RfsBeaconOrdersGui.lua`), **extract it first** into its own module with a header: `FROZEN` or `VOLATILE`.
3. Fix only the broken module. Do not commit frozen files for menu/rename/range/overlay/#6.

## Frozen vs volatile (do not mix)

-- FROZEN unless the user explicitly asks: battery spend (idle = no drain; 56s Hack), caps **base 4** (+ radio modules), hijack damage/HP (bots must take hits), Orders `queueOpen` / E / `cl_rfs_ordersOpen` open path.
- **VOLATILE**: Orders GUI widgets, rename labels, `/menu` names, Stay/Recall copy.
- **SHOW RANGE**: Game-hosted `RfsRangeViz` only. Never parent FX/`ShapeRenderable`/lights onto the beacon interactable (welds onto the electrical net and dumps the battery box). Do not “finish #6” by re-hosting on the beacon.

## Spend Lua is not the drain bug

`RfsHackBeacon` spend is bit-identical to `rush-base` (`75abb2f`). If batteries dump, look at hosted range FX or deploy overlay — do not retune `drainEvery`.

## Pack stamp

Bump `RFS_PACK_STAMP` in `Scripts/Game.lua` on **every** Workshop/Roaming copy (chat must change). Never ship two builds with the same stamp.

## Deploy

One play dest. Quit Scrap Mechanic, copy once (Workshop + Roaming). Do not treat GitHub vs Steam vs three local folders as “the code changed.”

**Always delete Cache after copy.** Scrap Mechanic keeps compiled Lua in Roaming `Cache\` (especially `Cache\Raw\*.rco`). A copy without wiping Cache can keep running the previous spend/`setActive` bytecode while chat shows a new pack stamp. After every Roaming/Workshop copy: delete the dest `Cache\` folder (or at least `Cache\Raw\`). Then relaunch.
